  "Number": 27,
  "Question": "A right circular cone has for its base a circle having the same radius as a given sphere. The volume of the cone is one-half that of the sphere. The ratio of the altitude of the cone to the radius of its base is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac11\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac12\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac23\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac21\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\sqrt{\\dfrac54}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Let \\(r>0\\) be both the sphere radius and the cone's base radius, and let \\(h\\) be the cone's altitude. Using the same \\(r\\) in both volume formulas makes the comparison direct:\n\\[\n\\frac13\\pi r^2h\n=\\frac12\\left(\\frac43\\pi r^3\\right)\n=\\frac23\\pi r^3.\n\\]\nDivide by the positive quantity \\(\\pi r^2/3\\) to obtain \\(h=2r\\). Therefore\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{h}{r}=\\frac21},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
